  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained rise in global fuel prices driven by disruptions in Middle Eastern energy markets increases import costs for major Western trading partners, provoking tariffs, emergency trade measures or disputes over contracts that manifest as increased bilateral trade tension.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">middle_east_energy</data>
  <data key="d39">western_alliance_realign</data>
