<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_engagement" target="middle_east_energy::military_deployment" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalation in Russia's military engagement prompts NATO, allied navies and regional powers to redeploy ships, aircraft and expeditionary forces to the Middle East to reassure partners and deter spillover, increasing regional force deployment intensity.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_energy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_engagement" target="space_weapons_race::counterspace_capability_" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">High‑intensity and visible battlefield use of space‑enabled ISR, targeting and comms in the Russia–Ukraine conflict prompts defense ministers to fast‑track funding and procurement of electronic warfare, satellite‑jamming, cyber and kinetic counterspace programs to deny adversary space support.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">space_weapons_race</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_engagement" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::geo_tension_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">A marked increase in kinetic operations widens perceptions of systemic instability and prompts faster, more adversarial strategic posturing by the US and China, raising bilateral geopolitical tension.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_engagement" target="western_alliance_realign::diplomatic_alignment" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalations in Russian kinetic operations raise threat perceptions among nearby and like‑minded states, driving them to publicly align diplomatically with the Western political‑economic union for security and sanctions coordination.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">western_alliance_realign</data>
</edge>
