<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::arms_flow_rate" target="middle_east_energy::energy_export_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased flows of weapons and munitions emerging from the conflict empower militias and non‑state actors in the Middle East to conduct more frequent sabotage and attacks on pipelines, terminals and loading infrastructure, degrading physical export capacity.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_energy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::arms_flow_rate" target="space_weapons_race::space_defense_production" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A surge in cross‑border arms transfers includes dual‑use components and creates demand for space‑capable sensors, EW pods and satellite survivability gear, incentivizing defense contractors to retool and raise production rates for space‑relevant systems.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">space_weapons_race</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::arms_flow_rate" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::regulatory_restrictions" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Documented increases in cross‑border arms transfers that involve or transit through Chinese-linked suppliers lead US regulators to impose targeted export controls and tightened licensing on dual‑use components and supply‑chain actors tied to China.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::arms_flow_rate" target="western_alliance_realign::integration_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained high-volume transfers of arms to Ukraine force recipient governments to harmonize export controls, certification and logistics procedures with partners, increasing institutional capacity to integrate policies and administration.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">western_alliance_realign</data>
</edge>
