<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::advanced_chip_capacity" target="russia_ukraine_war::drone_attack_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A fall in available advanced semiconductor production (domestic or accessible via trade) reduces the supply of flight‑control, guidance and sensor chips that Russia relies on, degrading procurement and repair of UAVs and thereby reducing the rate of drone attacks.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::advanced_chip_capacity" target="space_weapons_race::space_defense_production" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">An increase in available advanced semiconductor capacity eases a key bottleneck for manufacturing radios, guidance units, ASICs and phased-array components, allowing existing space-defense production lines to increase output without redesign.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">space_weapons_race</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::advanced_chip_capacity" target="space_weapons_race::counterspace_capability_" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">More advanced chips enable higher-performance on-board processing, EW payloads and seeker/GPS-denied guidance in new or upgraded platforms, directly raising the effective counterspace capabilities fielded.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">space_weapons_race</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::advanced_chip_capacity" target="western_alliance_realign::integration_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Addition of onshore or allied-node advanced fabs and associated supply infrastructure creates shared procurement options and technical commonalities that directly increase institutions' ability to integrate policies and administrative practices.</data>
  <data key="d37">12-36 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">western_alliance_realign</data>
</edge>
