<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::regulatory_restrictions" target="russia_ukraine_war::arms_flow_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter export controls and licensing by the US and partners on semiconductors and dual‑use tech restrict legal and illicit routing of Western components via third countries (including China), directly reducing Russia's ability to procure high‑end weapons components and lowering the volume/tempo of advanced arms deliveries.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::regulatory_restrictions" target="western_alliance_realign::regulatory_alignment" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Unilateral escalation of export controls, screening and licensing requirements forces partner states either to copy divergent restrictive regimes or to retain looser rules, reducing harmonization with external standards.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">western_alliance_realign</data>
</edge>
