<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::geo_tension_level" target="middle_east_energy::chokepoint_accessibility" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalating US–China geopolitical friction increases state-linked cyber and covert operations aimed at maritime traffic-management systems (AIS, VTS) and port infrastructure, producing temporary closures, navigation slowdowns, or reduced throughput at key chokepoints.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_energy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::geo_tension_level" target="middle_east_energy::fuel_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising strategic tension between the US and China increases market risk premia and speculative positioning in oil and refined-fuel futures as traders price higher odds of supply disruptions, producing upward pressure on global fuel prices.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_energy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::geo_tension_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising US–China strategic friction forces allied governments to reallocate diplomatic and operational attention and to adopt divergent economic/security stances, stressing Western political and operational unity on Russia policy and reducing alliance cohesion.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::geo_tension_level" target="space_weapons_race::orbital_weapons_density" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising geopolitical tension prompts governments to accelerate deployment of armed or weapon-capable payloads and co-orbital interceptors to orbit as deterrent and escalation signaling, raising the local density of weaponized objects.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">space_weapons_race</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::geo_tension_level" target="western_alliance_realign::trade_tension_partner" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Spikes in geopolitical tension rapidly translate into sanctions, tariff threats and administrative trade barriers used as levers of state competition, directly increasing bilateral trade friction.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">western_alliance_realign</data>
</edge>
