<edge source="space_weapons_race::orbital_weapons_density" target="middle_east_energy::chokepoint_accessibility" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Greater density of orbital weapons elevates the likelihood of on‑orbit incidents or attacks that could disable surveillance/navigation satellites, prompting coastal authorities and port/state control to impose conservative transit restrictions and temporary closures that reduce chokepoint throughput.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">space_weapons_race</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_energy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="space_weapons_race::orbital_weapons_density" target="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_disruption" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher numbers and concentration of orbital weapons raise the probability of kinetic tests/engagements and debris generation that disrupt earth‑observation, weather and communications satellites used for grid and pipeline monitoring, increasing interruptions to energy production and distribution.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">space_weapons_race</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="space_weapons_race::orbital_weapons_density" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::regulatory_restrictions" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A rising concentration of weapons in orbit prompts governments to tighten export controls, technology transfer rules, and partnership approvals for space‑relevant hardware and software to prevent proliferation and protect sensitive capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">space_weapons_race</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="space_weapons_race::orbital_weapons_density" target="western_alliance_realign::trade_tension_partner" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A rapid rise in concentrated orbital weapons deployments by one state causes its trading partners to impose targeted sanctions, export controls and supply‑chain restrictions on space and dual‑use goods, directly increasing bilateral trade friction.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">space_weapons_race</data>
  <data key="d39">western_alliance_realign</data>
</edge>
