<edge source="space_weapons_race::launch_cadence" target="space_weapons_race::basing_and_logistics_foo" id="0">
  <data key="d27">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="space_weapons_race::launch_cadence" target="middle_east_energy::energy_export_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">A marked uptick in launch cadence expands and more frequently activates range safety exclusion zones and temporary sea/air closures near launch sites, intermittently preventing tanker movements and terminal operations and reducing export throughput until procedures are adapted.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">space_weapons_race</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_energy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="space_weapons_race::launch_cadence" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_engagement" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">An elevated launch cadence for ISR and tactical communications payloads increases on‑orbit sensor and downlink capacity, improving targeting, battle‑management and strike coordination that enables higher frequency and precision of kinetic engagements on the battlefield.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">space_weapons_race</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="space_weapons_race::launch_cadence" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::tech_capital_inflow_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased and predictable launch activity enlarges addressable markets and lowers per‑launch unit costs, improving investment returns and attracting venture and institutional capital into space and adjacent tech supply chains.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">space_weapons_race</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="space_weapons_race::launch_cadence" target="western_alliance_realign::integration_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A sharp rise in national launch activity necessitates expanded joint space‑traffic management, licensing coordination and data‑sharing arrangements, forcing institutions to build administrative and technical capacity to integrate with external partners.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">space_weapons_race</data>
  <data key="d39">western_alliance_realign</data>
</edge>
