<edge source="space_weapons_race::counterspace_capability_" target="middle_east_energy::insurance_premium_avail" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A rapid increase in counterspace capabilities raises insurers' assessed risk of GNSS/comm outages and deliberate targeting of space-enabled maritime and energy systems, causing insurers to raise premiums and restrict coverage for shipments and facilities.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">space_weapons_race</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_energy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="space_weapons_race::counterspace_capability_" target="russia_ukraine_war::drone_attack_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">An increase in counterspace capabilities (jamming, RF denial, and ASAT operations) directly degrades satellite navigation and datalinks that many Ukrainian and Russian UAS depend on, reducing effective launches and on‑target employment of drones.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">space_weapons_race</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="space_weapons_race::counterspace_capability_" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::geo_tension_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">Visible tests or deployments of counter‑space systems directly increase perceived vulnerability of national C4ISR and communications satellites, provoking accelerated diplomatic escalation, threat declarations, and crisis signalling between the US and China.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">space_weapons_race</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="space_weapons_race::counterspace_capability_" target="western_alliance_realign::diplomatic_alignment" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">The emergence of advanced counter‑space capabilities by a strategic competitor drives affected states to coordinate and converge their diplomatic positions and collective policies within allied unions to present a unified deterrent and response posture.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">space_weapons_race</data>
  <data key="d39">western_alliance_realign</data>
</edge>
