<edge source="space_weapons_race::space_defense_production" target="middle_east_energy::military_deployment" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained increases in space‑defense production generate deliveries, training needs, and basing/logistics requirements that drive additional forward deployments, advisors, and force rotations into the Middle East to operate and protect new systems.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">space_weapons_race</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_energy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="space_weapons_race::space_defense_production" target="russia_ukraine_war::arms_flow_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A rapid ramp‑up in production of space‑defense systems reallocates industrial capacity, skilled labor and budgetary priority away from conventional munitions and platforms, slowing the tempo and volume of arms deliveries to the Ukraine theater.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">space_weapons_race</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="space_weapons_race::space_defense_production" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::advanced_chip_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher government procurement and production of space‑grade defense systems creates guaranteed demand and procurement subsidies that directly incentivize foundries and firms to expand or requalify advanced semiconductor manufacturing capacity domestically.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">space_weapons_race</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="space_weapons_race::space_defense_production" target="western_alliance_realign::regulatory_alignment" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained increase in domestic production of space defense systems prompts unilateral export controls, security screening and procurement offsets that create divergence from external regulatory standards and reduce harmonization with partner regimes.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">space_weapons_race</data>
  <data key="d39">western_alliance_realign</data>
</edge>
