<edge source="western_alliance_realign::trade_tension_partner" target="middle_east_energy::fuel_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalating trade frictions or sanctions between Western actors and a major energy supplier raise transaction costs and can directly restrict exports or chartering options, tightening supply and pushing up global fuel prices.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">western_alliance_realign</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_energy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="western_alliance_realign::trade_tension_partner" target="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_disruption" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalating trade frictions (tariffs, export controls or sanctions) with a major energy exporter provoke retaliatory cuts, transit restrictions or market disruptions that materially interrupt regional energy deliveries tied to the Russia–Ukraine theatre.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">western_alliance_realign</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="western_alliance_realign::trade_tension_partner" target="space_weapons_race::launch_cadence" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalating trade tensions trigger tariffs, export restrictions and supplier exclusions that immediately disrupt supply chains for rocket components and launch services, reducing launch frequency.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">western_alliance_realign</data>
  <data key="d39">space_weapons_race</data>
</edge>
<edge source="western_alliance_realign::trade_tension_partner" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::tech_capital_inflow_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising trade friction with a major partner raises political and commercial risk for investments in that partner's tech sector and prompts investors and governments to reallocate equity and subsidy flows toward domestic/allied semiconductor and tech projects, increasing capital inflows to rival (Western) tech ecosystems.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">western_alliance_realign</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
